            },
            "advisory": "Affected versions of the `pip` package are vulnerable to Inclusion of Functionality from Untrusted Control Sphere due to the deferred import of well-known Python module names. The self-update check functionality, which runs after installing wheel files, requires importing these modules, creating a risk if a newly-installed module with the same name is malicious. An attacker can exploit this by crafting a malicious package with module names that match those required by the self-update functionality, potentially executing arbitrary code upon installation.",
