            "advisory": "Affected versions of the Mako package are vulnerable to Path Traversal due to a mismatch between the posixpath-based URI normalisation used in TemplateLookup.get_template() and the Windows-native ntpath path resolution used by os.path.isfile() and os.path.normpath() in Template.__init__(). The get_template() method normalises the URI using posixpath, which treats backslashes as literal characters and thus fails to detect directory traversal sequences embedded via backslash separators, while os.path.normpath() in Template.__init__() resolves backslash-based .. sequences to a form that bypasses the startswith(\"..\") guard. An attacker who can supply a user-controlled template name or include path to TemplateLookup.get_template() on a Windows host can read arbitrary files outside the configured template directory, and if the targeted file contains Mako or Python template syntax, it may additionally be parsed and executed as a template.",
