            },
            "advisory": "Affected versions of the langchain-text-splitters package are vulnerable to Server-Side Request Forgery due to HTMLHeaderTextSplitter.split_text_from_url() validating only the initial URL with validate_safe_url() while performing the fetch with redirects enabled and without revalidating redirect targets. The method in libs/text-splitters/langchain_text_splitters/html.py passes the user-supplied URL through validate_safe_url(allow_private=False) and then calls requests.get() with the default follow-redirects behavior, so a public attacker-controlled host that returns an HTTP 302 to an internal address, localhost, or an unauthenticated cloud metadata endpoint such as AWS IMDSv1 causes the fetch to land on the internal target. An attacker who supplies such a URL to an application that invokes split_text_from_url() can coerce the server to retrieve internal resources and, if the calling application returns Document content to the requester, exfiltrate data from otherwise unreachable internal endpoints.",
